;; ============================================================
;; src/main.watx — THE source manifest for Wine-Assembly.
;;
;; This file is the ONE hand-maintained source order, and there is no longer a
;; copy of it anywhere. Everything that needs the order DERIVES it from here:
;;
;;   - lib/wat-manifest.js — parses the include list below. Every Node consumer
;;     reads it from there, including the WAT_FILES that lib/compile-wat.js
;;     still re-exports (a getter now, not an array of its own).
;;   - lib/watx-launcher.js — the browser fetches this file and parses the same
;;     list, so the page's source build uses no manifest but this one.
;;   - tools/concat-wat.js — writes build/combined.wat from that list, adding
;;     the outer (module ...) wrapper that no source fragment carries.
;;
;; TO ADD OR REORDER A PART: edit the include list HERE. That is the whole
;; procedure. Filename order (LC_ALL=C sort) is enforced by
;; tools/check-wat-manifest.js, which also catches the one thing the compiler
;; cannot: a src/*.wat that no (include ...) below names is not part of the
;; program, and nothing would otherwise say so.
;;
;; Include paths are relative to src/, so a driver populates the compiler's vfs
;; by reading src/<name> for each key.
;;
;; No fragment below contains a (module ...) wrapper: each balances its own
;; parentheses (gated by tools/check-wat-fragments.js), which is what lets the
;; WATX compiler's include resolver splice them as top-level module fields and
;; what lets lib/compile-wat.js parse each part independently.
;; ============================================================
